&lt;p&gt;If you've built an AI chat UI, you've seen this: the model streams half a code block, and suddenly your whole reply turns into a giant monospace mess. A &lt;code&gt;**&lt;/code&gt; opens bold and never closes. A link renders as &lt;code&gt;[text](htt&lt;/code&gt;. Then the next token arrives and everything jumps back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We hit this so often that we ended up building a component library around it: &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/anythic/anythic-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;anythic/ui&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, open-source React components for AI apps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The problem: Markdown is not designed to be incomplete
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Markdown parsers assume they get the whole document. During streaming, they only get a prefix:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Here is the fix:

```ts
function add(a, b) {
  return a +
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The code fence is open, so everything after it is treated as code, including text that hasn't arrived yet. With every token, the layout flips back and forth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The fix: repair the prefix before parsing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of rendering the raw prefix, we "complete" it first: close the open code fence, close unbalanced &lt;code&gt;**&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_&lt;/code&gt; and backticks, and hold back a link until its URL is complete. The parser always sees valid Markdown, so the reply grows smoothly instead of flickering.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In anythic/ui this happens inside the &lt;code&gt;Markdown&lt;/code&gt; component. You just pass the text as it streams:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Markdown&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@anythic/ui&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Markdown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;streamingText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Markdown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  The rest of an AI interface
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once Markdown worked, we kept going with the other pieces every agent UI needs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;ReasoningBlock&lt;/strong&gt;: collapsible "thinking" that shows how long the model thought&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;ToolCall&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;ToolApproval&lt;/strong&gt;: show what the agent is doing, and ask before dangerous actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Plan&lt;/strong&gt;: a live checklist of the agent's steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CodeDiff&lt;/strong&gt;: file changes with an in-house Myers diff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Terminal&lt;/strong&gt;: command output with an ANSI color parser and progress bars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Citation&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Sources&lt;/strong&gt;: numbered references that match &lt;code&gt;[1]&lt;/code&gt; in the text&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;PromptInput&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Conversation&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Message&lt;/strong&gt;: the chat shell itself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Everything is model-agnostic: components take plain props, so they work with the Vercel AI SDK, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini or your own backend. Styling uses Tailwind v4 with shadcn-compatible tokens, so it drops into existing shadcn projects and supports dark mode out of the box.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm i @anythic/ui
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The repo includes screenshots of every component and a demo app you can run locally with your own Gemini key:&lt;br&gt;
👉 &lt;a href="https://github.com/anythic/anythic-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/anythic/anythic-ui&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's MIT licensed. We'd love your feedback: what's the most annoying part of building AI UIs for you, and which component should we build next?**&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fu3v6au5rbqa7ji9qr1sp.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fu3v6au5rbqa7ji9qr1sp.png" alt=" " width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;**&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every reporting screen gets the same request after its first week: "Can I see this by month instead?" Then by product, then by country and month together. A pivot table is the answer that stops the requests, because the user drags the fields where they want them and gets the report they were about to ask for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The catch is the data. Every drag regroups and re-sums every row. With a few thousand rows nobody notices. With a million, the obvious implementation freezes the page while it works, and a page that freezes on every drag is a page people stop dragging in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post measures that on real data: the 1,067,371 invoice lines of the &lt;a href="https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/502" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Online Retail II&lt;/a&gt; dataset, pivoted in the browser with our free PivotGrid. The &lt;a href="https://kanunilabs.com/demos/pivot" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;demo&lt;/a&gt; times every recompute in your own browser, so you can check each number here against your machine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The report a user builds
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start from revenue by country and year, then drag Month into the columns or Product into the rows. Each drop recomputes the whole table:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F56vqporrfre20svnj9k3.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F56vqporrfre20svnj9k3.png" alt="Revenue and units by country and year, built from 1,067,371 invoice lines" width="799" height="455"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React that is one component and a list of fields; &lt;code&gt;area&lt;/code&gt; says where each field starts, and the user moves them from there:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BasePivotGrid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@kanunilabs/pivotgrid-react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@kanunilabs/pivotgrid-react/styles.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fields&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;country&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;country&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;caption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Country&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;row&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;caption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;caption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;summaryType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;caption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// waiting to be dragged&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataField&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;caption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BasePivotGrid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;gridId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"sales"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;initialFields&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fields&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  What a drag costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The demo measures two things on every recompute:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;How long it takes&lt;/strong&gt;, from the moment the pivot starts to the moment the new table is painted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The longest pause on the page's main thread&lt;/strong&gt; in that window. The browser's Long Tasks API reports every task of 50 ms or more, and the main thread is the one that also handles your clicks and keys. Rendering the new table counts too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For country by year, or sales against cancellations by country, a recompute took 29 to 48 ms and no task on the main thread reached 50 ms. Drag Month into the columns and Year out, about 40 countries by 25 months, and it took 45 to 82 ms over three runs, with the longest pause between none and 54 ms:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjxi174pumas70g5x8nar.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fjxi174pumas70g5x8nar.png" alt="The measurement panel after dragging Month into the columns: the recompute time and the longest main-thread pause" width="800" height="620"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The grouping and summing run in a Web Worker, a second thread the page starts for the pivot. The main thread only receives the finished totals and draws them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The obvious way, measured
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To see what the worker buys, the demo has a button that computes the same country-by-year revenue the way a quick implementation would: one pass over every row with a &lt;code&gt;Map&lt;/code&gt;, on the main thread.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;country&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That loop froze the page for about 110 ms, longer than the pivot's whole recompute. Its totals are the same as the pivot's: £7,511,064 for the United Kingdom in 2011 and £134,790 for France in 2010, which we also checked with an independent computation over the source file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A tenth of a second does not sound like much until you type through it. The demo has a text box for that: type while you drag fields, and the letters keep appearing; type while the loop runs, and they arrive all at once when it ends.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fs4tw8plvvxkq78ool2ww.gif" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fs4tw8plvvxkq78ool2ww.gif" alt="Two fields dragged with the mouse, each recompute timed in the panel; then the wide layout, and the plain loop on the main thread" width="600" height="464"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The worker does not make the work free. It moves it off the thread that answers the user.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where the page stopped, and the fix it led to
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Put Product in the rows and Month in the columns, about 5,000 products by 25 months, sorted by name, and the measurement changed: on October 7 the recompute took 350 to 650 ms and the main thread paused for 290 to 510 ms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The aggregation was still in the worker, so we looked at what was left on the main thread. Sorting the same table by revenue instead of by name cut the pause to 105 to 183 ms. The difference was how the 5,000 product names were compared:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// what the pivot's sort did before 1.7.2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;names&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;localeCompare&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;numeric&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the same order, with the collator built once&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;collator&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Intl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Collator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;numeric&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;names&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;collator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;compare&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Both give the same order. On 5,000 names, about 60,000 comparisons, the first took 206 to 226 ms and the second 4 to 5 ms, on the same machine. Called with an options object, &lt;code&gt;localeCompare&lt;/code&gt; sets up its comparison rules again on every call; a collator sets them up once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We shipped the second version in PivotGrid 1.7.2 on October 8 (&lt;code&gt;@kanunilabs/pivotgrid-react&lt;/code&gt; 1.4.2). Measured again in the live demo, five loads each, the layout sorted by name now takes 151 to 196 ms with a longest pause of 97 to 118 ms, the same as sorted by revenue. You can check it at &lt;a href="https://kanunilabs.com/demos/pivot?layout=product-month&amp;amp;sort=name" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;/demos/pivot?layout=product-month&amp;amp;sort=name&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you sort strings anywhere a user waits, a table header, a filter list, a dropdown, this one is worth checking in your own code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The remaining 100 or so milliseconds were in the React grid, not in the pivot. After the first paint it measured the panel widths and header heights and kept them in React state, so the roughly 1,400 visible cells were drawn a second time in the same task, only to change two paddings and a few CSS variables. It also wrote the row-header width variables on the grid's outer box, where every cell inherits them, so each write invalidated the style of every cell and the next measurement forced a full style recalculation. Now the measurements go through refs and the variables sit only on the panel that reads them. On a local production build of this demo, ten switches to Product × Month, the median longest pause went from 89 to 51 ms and the recompute from 155 to 102 ms. That fix shipped in &lt;code&gt;@kanunilabs/pivotgrid-react&lt;/code&gt; 1.5.0 on October 9.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5hgrpdsdmphimvqgi7iw.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5hgrpdsdmphimvqgi7iw.png" alt="Product by month, best sellers first: the measurement panel after the recompute" width="800" height="620"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Measure your own pivot
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do not need our component to get these two numbers. Any pivot or table that recomputes on user input can be measured the same way:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;longTasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PerformanceEntry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PerformanceObserver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;longTasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getEntries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()))&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;observe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;longtask&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;buffered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recompute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;                       &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// whatever your table does on a drag&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;          &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the new table has been painted&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pause&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;longTasks&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`recompute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; ms, longest main-thread pause &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; ms`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the second number is large, your users feel it, whatever the first one says.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What this costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It is free.&lt;/strong&gt; Drag and drop, filters, sorting, % of totals and saved views are in the Community package, with no licence key and no watermark. Calculated fields in code and the rows behind a clicked cell are free too; the formula designer for end users, rendered charts, the ready-made drill-down window and styled Excel/PDF export are in the paid edition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The data has to be in the browser.&lt;/strong&gt; The demo downloads a 5.5 MB file once and decodes it into a million row objects before the first pivot. For data that should stay on the server, the paid edition can ask your server for the aggregates instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Wide layouts still pause the page.&lt;/strong&gt; For 5,000 products by 25 months, after the two fixes above, the median longest pause was 51 ms on our local production build; slower machines see more. The panel in the demo shows what yours does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The demo is at &lt;a href="https://kanunilabs.com/demos/pivot" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;/demos/pivot&lt;/a&gt;; &lt;a href="https://kanunilabs.com/demos/pivot?layout=product-month" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;/demos/pivot?layout=product-month&lt;/a&gt; opens the wide layout, best sellers first, and adding &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;sort=name&lt;/code&gt; sorts it by name. The &lt;a href="https://kanunilabs.com/docs/pivotgrid" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PivotGrid docs&lt;/a&gt; cover fields, filters, summary types and the React and plain JavaScript setups.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Data: Online Retail II, UCI Machine Learning Repository (Chen, 2019), CC BY 4.0.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disclosure: this article was drafted with AI assistance. The demo and every number in it were measured against our packages and the published dataset in October 2026.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TL;DR: For a healthtech AI agent, choose error monitoring around rollback evidence, not feature count. Keep backend exceptions searchable and grouped beside release, latency, and cost context. Use a separate browser-focused product when source maps or session replay are required. This split makes a bad agent release easier to identify and reverse without pretending that one tool covers every diagnostic job.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A solo SaaS has a blunt constraint: every hour spent operating telemetry is an hour not spent shipping the next weekly release. I would therefore keep the ingestion contract tiny and make the provider replaceable. The clinical workflow raises the bar, though. An exception event may contain sensitive data, and a vendor that cannot support the required deletion and export workflow is disqualified before its dashboard gets a vote.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How should I pick an error tracking service for Next.js and React?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An AI agent loop can fail without throwing. It can also throw after several model calls have already accumulated latency and cost. Error tracking alone cannot measure that whole loop, so I would send exceptions to the error service while keeping latency and cost in the agent-run record. The join keys are a run ID and release ID. Those two fields answer the operational question: did this release change exception shape, total latency, or cost per completed run?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The smallest useful exception record has a stable fingerprint, an opaque run ID, a release ID, a stage, and a sanitized message. For a clinical intake agent, stages might be &lt;code&gt;classify&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;retrieve&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;draft&lt;/code&gt;. Do not send the prompt, patient name, email address, or raw model response just because the SDK accepts arbitrary context. Data minimization belongs in the adapter, where every caller gets the same policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rollback safety changes the choice. I need to search individual events, see which failures were grouped together, and compare the active release with its predecessor. I do not need a replay of a clinician's browser session for that decision. If client-side failures can block intake, however, source-map reversal and replay become a separate, legitimate requirement. This is the first trade-off: the simpler backend service is not ideal for browser forensics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That boundary matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the rollback trigger conservative. A single novel exception is evidence, not an automatic verdict. A release comparison should use enough completed runs for the signal to be meaningful, and a human should still be able to inspect the grouped events. No universal threshold follows from the tooling; traffic volume and clinical risk determine it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The smallest replaceable implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This client deliberately owns retry behavior while leaving search filters empty because none are declared in discovery. It uses one verified route, reads the key from the environment, sets the method explicitly, honors &lt;code&gt;Retry-After&lt;/code&gt; on HTTP 429, and surfaces every other non-success response. The returned data stays &lt;code&gt;unknown&lt;/code&gt;; no response fields need to be invented for a minimal connectivity check.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY is required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;infrai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;cc/v1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wait&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;milliseconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;milliseconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;searchErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/errors/search`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;Authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Bearer &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;429&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;retry-after&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isFinite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_000&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;250&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;wait&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;searchErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Error search failed (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;): &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;searchErrors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The absence of query parameters is intentional. The live discovery parameters do not declare filters for this route, so adding &lt;code&gt;release&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;runId&lt;/code&gt;, or patient-related fields to the URL would be guesswork. Capture should likewise follow the discovered request schema rather than a made-up universal error shape. Full exception text is often convenient, but convenience is a poor reason to copy clinical context into another system; preserve diagnostic detail only after defining redaction, retention, access, and erasure behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is another trap here: provider fallback is not the same as swallowing ingestion errors. The application should not fail a patient-facing request because telemetry is unavailable, yet it should expose that loss through a separate operational signal. A bounded queue and explicit delivery metric are better than an unbounded retry loop. Keep retries idempotent whenever the destination supports a client event ID.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Four services, four sensible boundaries
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No row is a universal winner. This comparison starts with the requested shape: searchable grouped backend exceptions for a European deployment, with simple integration and no requirement for replay. Product capabilities and data-processing terms change, so verify current region, retention, deletion, and subprocessors during procurement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Service&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Where it fits this build&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Boundary that changes the choice&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sentry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A strong candidate when the same team wants mature issue grouping and deeper browser diagnostics&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Its larger client-debugging surface may be more machinery than a backend-only agent needs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rollbar&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A credible cross-stack error-monitoring option with grouping and deploy-aware workflows&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Confirm the exact EU data controls and API workflow required by the healthtech deletion policy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bugsnag&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A credible choice when release stability and application errors are the main operating view&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Confirm that its browser diagnostics and governance controls match the precise workflow rather than assuming parity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Datadog&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A broad option when logs, traces, metrics, and error tracking should live in one operations suite&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Its platform scope can exceed the needs of a small backend-only agent service&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Grafana&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A sensible evaluation candidate when an existing observability stack and flexible dashboards drive the decision&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;It is a stack choice, not a drop-in substitute for every dedicated browser-debugging workflow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Infrai&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Fits backend-focused ingestion where grouped issues and individual events must be available through a simple API; its broader 295-route, 20-module surface also keeps other backend capabilities under one contract&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;It has no source-map reversal or session replay, no alert or notification route, and no per-user log deletion API or bulk log export/subscription API&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sentry documents how fingerprints and grouping enhancements affect issue grouping. That is useful because a bad fingerprint can combine unrelated stages and hide a release-specific regression. Rollbar and Bugsnag deserve a proof-of-work against the same sanitized fixtures, not a decision based on screenshots. Test grouping stability, search by release and run ID, event retrieval, regional processing terms, and deletion behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Infrai provides one REST API for the entire backend: one key, one wallet, and one bill cover 295 routes across 20 modules, so there are no dozens of SDKs, keys, or invoices to manage. Any language or runtime can call the plain HTTP interface without installing an SDK. Adding another production capability can remain another endpoint under the same contract. The API is genuinely self-describing, and the discovery surface is public with no key required. That surface provides request and response schemas and runnable examples, so the integration can be generated from declared paths. The limitation is material. It is not suitable when source-map reversal, session replay, built-in notifications, or per-user log deletion is mandatory, and Sentry is the stronger candidate here when rich frontend diagnosis drives the purchase.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is the fair dividing line. Rollbar and Bugsnag belong in the evaluation when a conventional dedicated error-monitoring product is preferred. Datadog or Grafana makes more sense when errors must join a broader observability estate. The narrower backend API is attractive when integration breadth and a small operational surface matter more than replay, source maps, or built-in notifications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No dashboard erases that trade-off.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ship the boundary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How I would test the rollback path
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would run a two-release fixture through every candidate. Release A emits two instances of the same sanitized &lt;code&gt;TypeError&lt;/code&gt; during &lt;code&gt;retrieve&lt;/code&gt;; release B emits one &lt;code&gt;TypeError&lt;/code&gt; during &lt;code&gt;retrieve&lt;/code&gt; and one distinct timeout during &lt;code&gt;draft&lt;/code&gt;. These are test inputs, not production measurements. The expected result is two stable groups, with every event searchable by its release and opaque run ID.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then I would rehearse the actual decision. Can I isolate release B, inspect the new group, link it to the agent-run latency and cost record, and switch traffic back without changing telemetry code? Can I delete data according to the written policy? Can I export what compliance and incident review require? A polished issue page does not compensate for a no on any mandatory question.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alerts need equal scrutiny. The backend-focused API described above has no threshold, phone, SMS, or webhook notification route, so detection requires polling its free query surface and operating an external notifier. It also has no synthetic or heartbeat monitoring. A scheduled agent job that silently never starts therefore needs a tool such as Healthchecks, regardless of how well thrown exceptions are grouped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Distributed tracing is outside this choice too. Logs can carry &lt;code&gt;trace_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;span_id&lt;/code&gt;, but there is no distributed-trace query or span tree. If the agent loop must explain latency across model, retrieval, and database calls, evaluate a tracing system separately instead of treating error events as spans.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Errors are not traces.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What changes at scale
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At low volume, the provider adapter, agent-run table, and a manual rollback are enough. At higher volume I would add a durable bounded queue, delivery counters, sampling for repeated low-value events, and an automated release comparison that proposes rather than executes a rollback. The weekly shipping rhythm survives because these pieces remain outside the product path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would also revisit the split if frontend support load grows. Once minified browser stacks consume real hours, source maps become an operating requirement. Once reproducing UI state dominates diagnosis, replay may justify its privacy review. Those are workload changes, not proof that the original backend-first choice was wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The decision rule is compact: &lt;strong&gt;pick the smallest service that preserves the evidence needed to reverse a release, passes the written data lifecycle, and leaves browser and tracing work to tools designed for them.&lt;/strong&gt; For this healthtech agent, searchable grouped backend exceptions are one input to rollback safety. Latency, cost, silent-job monitoring, and client diagnostics remain separate signals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Further reading
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sentry, event grouping and fingerprints: &lt;a href="https://docs.sentry.io/concepts/data-management/event-grouping/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.sentry.io/concepts/data-management/event-grouping/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rollbar documentation: &lt;a href="https://docs.rollbar.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.rollbar.com/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bugsnag documentation: &lt;a href="https://docs.bugsnag.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.bugsnag.com/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Datadog Error Tracking documentation: &lt;a href="https://docs.datadoghq.com/error_tracking/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.datadoghq.com/error_tracking/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grafana documentation: &lt;a href="https://grafana.com/docs/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://grafana.com/docs/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenTelemetry trace specification: &lt;a href="https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/trace/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/trace/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthchecks documentation: &lt;a href="https://healthchecks.io/docs/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://healthchecks.io/docs/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Martin Fowler, Feature Toggles: &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/articles/feature-toggles.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://martinfowler.com/articles/feature-toggles.html&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server-side validation catches bad emails before they hit your database, but by then the user has already submitted the form and is waiting on a response. If you want to tell someone their email looks undeliverable &lt;em&gt;while they're still typing&lt;/em&gt;, that's a different problem — and Next.js's API routes make it pretty clean to solve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's how I wired real-time validation into a signup flow, from the client-side debounce to the API route doing the actual check.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 1: The Basic Signup Form
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Starting point — a simple form with client-side state:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SignupForm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emailStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setEmailStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 'checking' | 'valid' | 'invalid' | null&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"you@company.com"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emailStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;checking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Checking...&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emailStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;invalid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;This email doesn't look deliverable&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emailStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;✓ Looks good&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Right now nothing actually populates &lt;code&gt;emailStatus&lt;/code&gt;. That's the part we're adding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 2: Debouncing the Check
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don't want to fire a validation request on every keystroke. A simple debounce hook handles that:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebounce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setDebounced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setDebounced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then hook it into the form:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;debouncedEmail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebounce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debouncedEmail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debouncedEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setEmailStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;checking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/verify-email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;debouncedEmail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setEmailStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;invalid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setEmailStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debouncedEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now the check fires 600ms after the user stops typing, not on every character.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 3: The API Route
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the Next.js API route the form is calling. Keep the actual validation logic server-side — never expose your validation API key to the client:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/api/verify-email/route.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;reason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;missing_email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validateEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;invalid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Email validation error:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// fail open — don't block signup over a validation service hiccup&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;valid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validateEmail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`https://api.gamalogic.com/v1/verify?email=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;amp;api_key=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;GAMALOGIC_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I'm using &lt;a href="https://gamalogic.com/email-validation/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Gamalogic's real-time email validation API&lt;/a&gt; here since it returns catch-all and disposable-domain detection alongside the basic valid/invalid check, which is more than a plain MX lookup gives you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 4: Handling the Loading and Error States Properly
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few things I got wrong on my first pass, worth calling out:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Don't block form submission on a pending check.&lt;/strong&gt; If the debounce hasn't resolved yet when the user hits submit, either wait briefly for it or re-validate server-side on submit — don't just let it through silently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fail open, not closed.&lt;/strong&gt; If the validation API times out or errors, treat the email as valid rather than blocking a real signup over an infrastructure blip. Log the failure so you can investigate separately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Debounce delay matters more than it looks.&lt;/strong&gt; Too short (under 300ms) and you're firing requests on every pause; too long (over 1s) and it feels laggy. 500-600ms was the sweet spot for me.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 5: Putting It Together on Submit
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;preventDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emailStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;invalid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// don't let obviously bad emails through&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/signup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// redirect or show success&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;/api/signup&lt;/code&gt; route should still re-run validation server-side rather than trusting the client-side &lt;code&gt;emailStatus&lt;/code&gt; — the client check is a UX nicety, not a security boundary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Real-time validation is mostly a UX problem wrapped around a server-side check you probably already have. Debounce the input, keep the actual validation call server-side, and decide up front how you want to handle a validation-service failure so a slow API doesn't turn into blocked signups.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Quest Begins (The "Why")
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Honestly, I was just trying to get a simple blog feature working. I had a list of posts, and for each post I wanted to show the comments. Seemed harmless, right? I wrote something like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight ruby"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;each&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nb"&gt;puts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nb"&gt;puts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;comments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I hit refresh, watched the server logs, and my heart sank. One query to fetch all posts, then a separate query for every single post to grab its comments. If I had 100 posts, that was 101 queries hitting the database. My page went from snappy to sluggish in a blink. I felt like I was stuck in a loop, watching the same nightmare repeat over and over. That’s when I knew I had to slay the N+1 dragon before it ate my performance for breakfast.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Revelation (The Insight)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The breakthrough came when I remembered how eager loading works. Instead of letting each loop iteration trigger its own query, I could tell the ORM to fetch the related data upfront. It felt like when the hero dodges bullets in &lt;em&gt;The Matrix&lt;/em&gt;—everything slowed down just enough for me to see the pattern and act.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is dead simple: add an &lt;code&gt;includes&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;joins&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;preload&lt;/code&gt; depending on your stack) to the original query. Suddenly, the ORM issues two queries total—one for the posts, one for all their comments—and then stitches them together in memory. No more surprise queries hiding in the loop. The page went from crawling back to sprinting, and I felt like I’d just unlocked a secret level.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Wielding the Power (Code &amp;amp; Examples)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The Trap: Naive Loop
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight ruby"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# app/controllers/posts_controller.rb&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;index&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="vi"&gt;@posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight erb"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- app/views/posts/index.html.erb --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="vi"&gt;@posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;each&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;comments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;each&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/ul&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="cp"&gt;&amp;lt;%&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;%&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every &lt;code&gt;@post.comments&lt;/code&gt; call fires off a fresh &lt;code&gt;SELECT * FROM comments WHERE post_id = ?&lt;/code&gt;. With 50 posts, you get 51 queries. Ouch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The Victory: Eager Loading
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight ruby"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# app/controllers/posts_controller.rb&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;index&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="vi"&gt;@posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:comments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The view stays exactly the same. Behind the scenes, Rails now runs:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;comments&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;IN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* all post ids */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Two queries, no matter how many posts you have. If you need even tighter control—say you only want the comment count—you can go further with a &lt;code&gt;LEFT JOIN&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;GROUP BY&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight ruby"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="vi"&gt;@posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;Post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;left_joins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;:comments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
             &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'posts.*, COUNT(comments.id) AS comment_count'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
             &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'posts.id'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now each post object comes with a &lt;code&gt;comment_count&lt;/code&gt; attribute, and you never touch the comments table unless you actually need the comment text. It’s like swapping a broadsword for a precise rapier—lighter, faster, and just as deadly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Common Pitfalls to Avoid
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forgot the association name&lt;/strong&gt; – &lt;code&gt;includes(:comment)&lt;/code&gt; (singular) won’t match the &lt;code&gt;has_many :comments&lt;/code&gt; declaration; Rails will ignore it and you’ll still see N+1. Double‑check the spelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Over‑eager loading&lt;/strong&gt; – Loading associations you never use wastes memory. If you only need the count, use a join or a counter cache instead of pulling in every comment row.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lazy loading inside a view helper&lt;/strong&gt; – Sometimes a helper method calls &lt;code&gt;@post.comments.size&lt;/code&gt; behind the scenes, re‑introducing the query. Keep an eye on any method that touches the association.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why This New Power Matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;N+1 queries are silent performance killers. They look fine in dev with a handful of records, but explode in production. By mastering eager loading (and its cousins—joins, preload, counter caches), you turn a potential bottleneck into a predictable, scalable pattern. Your pages stay snappy, your database stays happy, and you can focus on building features instead of firefighting latency spikes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;More than that, understanding this concept teaches you to think about data access patterns holistically. You start asking: “What do I really need to fetch right now?” That mindset leads to better API design, smarter caching strategies, and ultimately, faster, more reliable applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Your Turn
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s a challenge: grep your codebase for &lt;code&gt;.each&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;.map&lt;/code&gt; loops that touch an association. Run a quick benchmark with &lt;code&gt;bullet&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;rack-mini-profiler&lt;/code&gt; to see the N+1 count. Then apply &lt;code&gt;includes&lt;/code&gt; (or a join) and watch the query count drop. Share your before/after numbers in the comments—I’d love to hear how your quest went!  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Happy optimizing, and may your queries always be swift!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  🚀 Building GymFlow: A Full-Stack Gym Management Platform
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hey developers! 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I've been working on &lt;strong&gt;GymFlow&lt;/strong&gt;, a full-stack gym management platform designed to simplify the daily operations of gyms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea started with a simple question:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What if a gym could manage its members, memberships, payments, and daily operations from one place — while also having its own professional website?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That question inspired me to build GymFlow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  🛠️ Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's what I'm using to build the application:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; Next.js, React, TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Styling:&lt;/strong&gt; Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Database:&lt;/strong&gt; PostgreSQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;ORM:&lt;/strong&gt; Prisma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Authentication:&lt;/strong&gt; Custom session-based authentication using JWTs and HTTP-only cookies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Zod&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forms:&lt;/strong&gt; React Hook Form&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  ✨ Key Features
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  👥 Member Management
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Manage gym members and access their membership details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  📅 Membership &amp;amp; Subscription Management
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create membership plans, track subscriptions, and monitor expiration dates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  💳 Payment Management
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Track payments, payment statuses, and refunds while maintaining transaction history.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  🏋️ Attendance Tracking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Record attendance and monitor daily gym activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  💰 Financial Management
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Track gym income and expenses to help owners understand their finances.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  🔐 Role-Based Access Control
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Separate owner and staff permissions to protect sensitive operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  🧠 Some Things I'm Learning
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building GymFlow has taught me that developing a real-world application involves much more than creating UI components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some challenges I'm working through include:&lt;/p&gt;

